 79\\tassumption needs support from that contract or enforced validation; disclosing\\n    80\\tan assumption alone cannot establish a clean result when accepted inputs break\\n    81\\tthe guarantee. Record a concrete counterexample and classify its consequence\\n    82\\tunder the governing contract.\\n    83\\t\\n    84\\tFor each finding, cite exact code/contract locations, concrete evidence and\\n    85\\tconsequence, classify blocking versus optional, and give a proportionate remedy.\\n    86\\tA documented ownership breach can block even in unchanged code when it defeats\\n    87\\tthe ticket's approved outcome. A preference for classes, shorter functions or a\\n    88\\tparticular file layout alone is insufficient. A long cohesive function may be\\n    89\\tclean when its callers cross a small interface and it owns its decisions without\\n    90\\texternal coordination; explain that reasoning for the inspected flow.\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\tKeep the summary concise and link detail as needed. There is no universal short\\n    93\\treport cap: preserve all required scope, evidence and reasoning. Empty findings\\n    94\\tmean no findings within the recorded inspection, not universal design approval.\\n    95\\t\\n    96\\tFor cumulative milestone scope and start/post-implementation risk triggers, apply\\n    97\\t[architecture checkpoints](architecture-checkpoints.md). That contract determines\\n    98\\twhen broader work gates progression; this contract owns its substantive inspection.\\n    99\\t\\n   100\\t## Repair and handoff\\n   101\\t\\n   102\\tCarry the full review/report/local finding keys, original reports, disposition\\n   103\\thistory, approved contracts and exact rejected source to a fresh repair assignment.\\n   104\\tRecord its changed/unchanged ownership, claimed fixes and checks. Independently\\n   105\\tverify each claimed fix against the exact repaired revision and re-review the\\n   106\\twhole implementation from the original baseline using fresh separate axes.\\n   107\\tPreserve original reports and append verification/disposition events under the\\n   108\\t[record contract](review-records.md#immutable-reports-and-append-only-history).\\n   109\\tSource changes require relevant exact-source revalidation; historical clean\\n   110\\treports retain their original scope. Optional suggestions remain optional.\\n   111\\t\\n   112\\tA handoff links current ownership contracts/affected flows, assessment scope,\\n   113\\toriginal baseline/current source, unresolved full keys, missing reports, pending\\n   114\\trevalidation and human decisions with the responsible next action. State an\\n   115\\texplicit absence when none exists. Preserve active-run inputs, prior evidence,\\n   116\\tauthorized scope and milestone boundaries. Review completion and risk disposition\\n   117\\tremain separate from integration eligibility and human QA acceptance.\\n\"}}}\n{\"path\":\"guidance/docs/agents/review-records.md\",\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"f1d107\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.015860451,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2433,\"output\":\"     1\\t# Review records\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tUse this development record contract when preparing review assignments, saving\\n     4\\treports, disposing findings or carrying review context into a repair/handoff.\\n     5\\tIt implements the local [review contract](../../.scratch/ticket-harness/spec.md#review-work-findings-and-decisions)\\n     6\\tunder the existing [tracker conventions](issue-tracker.md). It defines Markdown\\n     7\\trecords, not a runtime report schema, scheduler or additional review gate.\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tBefore assigning source reviews or carrying ownership concerns into repairs or\\n    10\\thandoffs, apply [ownership and review scope](ownership-review.md). It owns the\\n    11\\tsubstantive cross-module inspection and reporting contract; these records own\\n    12\\tidentity, preservation and disposition